WEBVTT

00:00:09,360 --> 00:00:13,800
Do you recommend repeating Dutch test periodically?

00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:18,300
Absolutely, because, well, your cortisol level is going to change.

00:00:18,300 --> 00:00:21,800
And I will say this, if you're going to do a cortisol test,

00:00:21,800 --> 00:00:25,560
either through the Dutch test or the adrenal stress profile,

00:00:25,560 --> 00:00:31,420
you really have to do it on a day that's a normal day.

00:00:31,420 --> 00:00:36,520
Because if your normal is fairly in your mind, fairly

00:00:36,520 --> 00:00:42,280
stress-free, but then you had a super stressful day.

00:00:42,280 --> 00:00:44,720
And it's going to show.

00:00:44,720 --> 00:00:47,600
And then on that day, you do the adrenal stress profile.

00:00:47,600 --> 00:00:49,440
It's not going to be a real test.

00:00:49,440 --> 00:00:53,840
You want to do it on what you would consider your normal day.

00:00:53,840 --> 00:00:55,400
It might be very stressful.

00:00:55,400 --> 00:00:57,960
But if that's, if you're under a lot of stress all the time,

00:00:57,960 --> 00:01:05,280
you want to know what your cortisol levels are on an average time.

00:01:05,280 --> 00:01:11,800
So if it was just a day full of stress,

00:01:11,800 --> 00:01:15,880
and you run it, then you lose the value of it.

00:01:15,880 --> 00:01:17,000
So you lose them out.

00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:22,120
Because your cortisol levels are going to go up and down

00:01:22,120 --> 00:01:24,160
depending on your stress levels.

00:01:24,160 --> 00:01:28,440
Your cortisol is released by your adrenal glands

00:01:28,440 --> 00:01:30,680
and functions on many different levels.

00:01:30,680 --> 00:01:33,680
And on one of the levels, it's a breakdown

00:01:33,680 --> 00:01:34,920
like it in stores.

